# ── P34.18 / ADR-178 (S0 RI-01; B-3, OD-17, OD-20) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commits a58fa2fa and d130b54d are the verifier-backed bulk re-key the ticket's acceptance
# criterion demands (zero handle-list entries in the repo tip's tracked files): a Part VIII
# personal-data redaction across protected records — run ledgers, pr ledgers, the LEDGER PHASE
# LOG, DEFERRALS rows, planning records, and two landed-ADR body strings — each redaction
# recorded in-place and disclosed by the dated correction note
# (docs/governance/identifier-rekey-note.md); the appended ADR notes land as conforming
# `## Status updates` sections and the re-keyed DEFERRALS rows carry `as-of` markers. Their
# verifier is docs/build/tools/handle_crawl_check.py (0 hits, counts only). Same mechanism as
# the Stage-B seeds: corrective commits whose append-only findings are sanctioned, keyed by
# prefix so no later commit can borrow them — memory_guard strips only findings *attributed*
# to a declared commit, wherever it sits in a judged range.
seed-commit a58fa2fa
seed-commit d130b54d
